<BaseLayout title="My Story | Tony Adragna" description="Husband, dad of three, SVP of Operations at Keyholder Vacations, and head boys' basketball coach at Greenwood Christian Academy.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="kicker-line"></span>My Story</p>
      <h1>Husband. Dad. Leader. <span style="color:var(--orange)">Coach.</span></h1>
      <p>
        Everything I do runs on the same engine: people. Here's the longer version
        of how a point guard from the south side of Indianapolis ended up leading a
        company by day and a basketball program by night.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="prose">
    <h2>Husband &amp; Father</h2>
    <p>
      I met Jessica in the summer of 2007, heading into my junior year of high
      school. We talked here and there through the summer and fall, and that winter
      I finally decided to shoot my shot and ask her out. Best shot I ever took. We
      married in May 2015, and growing up alongside my high school sweetheart has
      been one of the greatest gifts of my life.
    </p>
    <p>
      In February 2020, after a painful pregnancy loss and months of trying, we
      welcomed our first child, Giovanni. Gio is full of personality, curiosity,
      and heart. Luciana followed in December 2021, and her personality is second
      to none; she marches to the beat of her own drum and we wouldn't have it any
      other way. Our third, Lorenzo (Enzo to everyone who knows him) arrived in
      August 2024 and has been the sweetest addition: laid back, expressive, and
      quickly developing his own little personality.
    </p>
    <p>
      Family means everything to me. No matter what else I accomplish, they will
      always come first.
    </p>

    <h2>Business Leader</h2>
    <p>
      Entrepreneurship is in my blood. My dad has owned and operated his own house
      painting business my entire life (and still does!). My own first venture came
      at age four, when I'd put on a suit and tie, take people's rocks out of their
      driveways, then knock on their door and sell them their rocks back for a
      penny each. Closing rate: surprisingly high.
    </p>
    <p>
      In 2019 I joined DVC Rental Store, the largest Disney Vacation Club
      point-rental broker in the United States, to run digital marketing, and kept
      raising my hand for more until I was overseeing operations too. In
      2020, in the middle of a pandemic that froze the travel industry, I was named
      President. Leading a team of more than 20 people through that season taught
      me more about leadership than any book could, though I read plenty of those
      too.
    </p>
    <p>
      In January 2026 I stepped into a new challenge as Senior Vice President of
      Operations at Keyholder Vacations, where I lead the people, processes, and
      systems that power our guests' vacations.
    </p>

    <h2>Basketball Coach</h2>
    <p>
      I grew up a point guard at Southport High School, on one of the best
      high school basketball scenes in the entire country. Three years on varsity,
      captain my senior year, and a basketball junkie ever since. At Indiana
      University I majored in sports broadcasting to stay close to the game,
      covering IU basketball as a student journalist, including rushing the court
      after The Shot against Kentucky.
    </p>
    <p>
      I started coaching at Southport Middle School in 2013 at age 23. My first
      team won three games. By year three, we broke the school's wins record. From
      there I moved up to the Southport High School staff, assisting across grades
      7-12: practices, scouting, player development. I stepped away after the 2019
      season to focus on family and career, and scratched the basketball itch by
      founding IU Film Room, a site dedicated to breaking down film on IU
      basketball.
    </p>
    <p>
      In 2025, I got the call I'd been waiting for: Head Boys' Basketball Coach at
      Greenwood Christian Academy. In our first season together, the Cougars won
      the 2026 IHSAA Class A sectional championship and advanced to regionals,
      playing our best basketball when it mattered most. We're just getting
      started.
    </p>

    <h2>Why I Write</h2>
    <p>
      This site is where the two halves of my life meet. Coaching made me a better
      executive; leading a company made me a better coach. I write about
      leadership: the lessons in the books, the ones in the gym, and the ones my
      kids teach me for free.
    </p>
    <p>
      Want to talk leadership, coaching, or hoops? Email me at
